Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: You should not use levothyroxine if you have an untreated or uncontrolled adrenal gland disorder.
You should not use certain liquid or injectable forms of levothyroxine if you are allergic to glycerin or edetate disodium.
To make sure this medicine is safe for you, tell your doctor if you have ever had:
- a thyroid nodule;
- thyroiditis (inflammation of the thyroid gland);
- heart problems such as a heart attack, stroke, angina, or an irregular heartbeat;
- a blood clot or a blood clotting disorder;
- diabetes (your diabetes medicine may need to be adjusted);
- anemia (low red blood cells);
- weak bones (osteoporosis), or low bone mineral density;
- problems with your pituitary or adrenal gland;
- an allergy to any food or drugs;
- recently received radiation therapy with iodine (such as I-131); or
- kidney disease.
Triplet: ["levothyroxine", "requires adjustment of", "diabetes medicine"]

The relation 'requires adjustment of' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug may necessitate changes in the dosage or management of the medication specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'may require dose adjustment': The subject medication might need a change in dosage under certain conditions or over time.
B. 'has dosage form': The subject drug is available in the pharmaceutical dosage form specified by the object entity.
C. 'has recommended dose': The subject drug is typically prescribed at the dose or dosing regimen specified by the object entity.
D. 'has side effect': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect or symptom specified by the object entity.
E. 'treats': The subject drug is used to treat or manage the disease or medical condition specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
